From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: Check the out pointer of the sink class factory.

The sink class factory wrote the new sink through a NULL pointer; a NULL
out pointer now gives E_POINTER (MFCreateMPEG4MediaSink(..., NULL) already
expected that from the mf tests, which return before reaching it).
---
 dlls/winegstreamer/media_sink.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winegstreamer/media_sink.c b/dlls/winegstreamer/media_sink.c
index 6a6e540..8822965 100644
--- a/dlls/winegstreamer/media_sink.c
+++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/media_sink.c
@@ -1715,6 +1715,9 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI sink_class_factory_create_media_sink(IMFSinkClassFactory *
     TRACE("iface %p, bytestream %p, video_type %p, audio_type %p, out %p.\n",
             iface, bytestream, video_type, audio_type, out);
 
+    if (!out)
+        return E_POINTER;
+
     if (FAILED(hr = media_sink_create(bytestream, format, &media_sink)))
         return hr;
     media_sink_iface = &media_sink->IMFFinalizableMediaSink_iface;
